  "releaseNotes": "1.1.6 - Rebuild with latest MailKit package to fix vulnerability.\n\t\t\t1.1.5 - Rebuild with new extension methods for Base64 encoding and decoding.\n\t\t\t1.1.4 - Rebuild with support for dates outside standard Unix epoch range.\n\t\t\t1.1.3 - Rebuild with added HTML and URL encode and decode methods.\n\t\t\t1.1.2 - Rebuild with reusable retry strategy.\n\t\t\t1.1.1 - Rebuild with updated utility extensions.\n\t\t\t1.1.0 - Rebuild with updated duration computation.\n\t\t\t1.0.17 - Loggers are non-nullable.\n\t\t\t1.0.16 - Rebuild with updated interfaces.\n\t\t\t1.0.15 - Rebuild with date/time extension methods for Unix epoch conversions.\n\t\t\t1.0.14 - Rebuild with Unix epoch extension methods.\n\t\t\t1.0.13 - Rebuild with geographic coordinate obfuscation.\n\t\t\t1.0.12 - Ability to add image source and embedded content.\n\t\t\t1.0.11 - Rebuild with default timestamp for service result.\n\t\t\t1.0.10 - Rebuild with enum extension methods.\n\t\t\t1.0.9 - Rebuild with type for geographic coordinates.\n\t\t\t1.0.8 - Rebuild with optional leading/trailing whitespace in key-value pair lookup.\n\t\t\t1.0.7 - Update third-party NuGet packages.\n\t\t\t1.0.6 - Rebuild with new metadata method.\n\t\t\t1.0.5 - Rebuild with updated time unit enum.\n\t\t\t1.0.4 - Rebuild with updated time unit enum.\n\t\t\t1.0.3 - Rebuild with updated interface for string conversion methods.\n\t\t\t1.0.2 - Initial revision, targetting .NET 8",
